--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
PARITY ARITHMETIC (reproduced exactly from the web source — cross-platform value parity, NOT "corrected")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  WidgetComparisonCard.tsx renders `visible = compact ? metrics.slice(0,2) : metrics`; `visible.length
  === 0` → "No comparison data"; otherwise one `MetricRow` per metric: the label, `formattedCurrent`
  (+ optional unit), and `<Delta metric={{direction}} current previous display="percent" size="sm">`
  where direction = higherIsBetter ? 'higher_better' : 'lower_better'.

  Delta.tsx (display = "percent"), ported 1:1 in WidgetComparisonDelta.resolve:
    missing input (current/previous null or non-finite) → em-dash, neutral, NO arrow.
    else signed = current - previous
         arrow   = signed > 0 up / signed < 0 down / 0 flat
         percent = previous != 0 ? fmtNumber(|signed / |previous|| * 100, 1) + "%" : nil  (nil → "—")
         tone    = signed == 0 muted; else (higher && +) || (lower && −) ? emerald : rose
    The arrow is shown even when the percent is em-dash (previous == 0 branch); only the missing-input
    guard hides it. The magnitude is always rendered positive — the arrow encodes the sign.
  fmtNumber → NumberFormatter(.decimal, grouped, halfUp); non-finite collapses to 0 (web `safeNumber`).

  Pinned by EXECUTED asserts (host harness, 54 checks):
    up/higher  312.4 vs 250  → "25.0%" ↑ emerald · clause "trending up 25.0%"
    down/lower 180   vs 200  → "10.0%" ↓ emerald (good) · clause "trending down 10.0%"
    down/higher 1234 vs 1500 → "17.7%" ↓ rose (grouping + half-away-from-zero)
    flat       45.6  vs 45.6 → "0.0%"  → muted · clause "no change"
    prev=0     268   vs 0    → "—" ↑ rose (lower-is-better) / emerald (higher) · clause "no prior data"
    missing    NaN   vs 5    → "—" muted, NO arrow
    fmt 1234.5→"1,235" · 24.96→"25.0" · 0.05→"0.1" · ∞→"0.0" · NaN→"0"
    projector: 4 rows ordered; "312 mi" / "12" (no unit) / "45.6 kWh" / "268 Wh/mi"; a11y
               "Distance, 312 mi, trending up 25.0%" … "Efficiency, 268 Wh/mi, no prior data";
               compact slice → [Distance, Drives]; [] → empty; duplicate labels → ids [0,1] (position);
               unit "" → nil. state resolve: [] → .empty ; non-empty → .content. summary([]) → message.

